From 1fa8240f81510eb1288b342a56d0e2222a3037e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ferdausfs <umuhammadiswa@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 10:28:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(push): restore auto signal delivery from the */5 scanner
 (F3-14 revert)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause: F3-14 added noPush:true to scanOnePair while the bot still had
its own autoScan; bot v4.5.0 then removed autoScan (worker = single source
of truth), leaving pushSignalToSubscribers with exactly one call site — the
manual /api/signal path. The scanner saved history rows but never delivered
them: auto signals stopped reaching Telegram subscribers.

Fix (Option B): drop noPush:true so the scanner rides the existing
handleSignalRaw -> saveAndPush chain. Push fires exactly when a NEW
tradeable row lands in history (30-min setup dedup), and claimPushLock
(30-min per subscriber/pair/direction) makes manual/scanner double-push
impossible in both orders. Scanner still writes only the latest: cache —
no double save.

Tests: T27 rewritten from the F3-14 grep contract to a behavioral test
(scanOnePair -> real engine -> Telegram stub): fresh tradeable signal
pushed once; re-scan not re-pushed; manual-after-scanner not re-pushed;
manual-first-then-scanner not re-pushed; pushLog/pushLock/history verified.
fix_tests 281/0; phase10 19/19; phase7 36/0 (+smoke 68/0); d2 39/39;
probe 34/34; entry_hit 7/7; fx_mode 20/20; r71 117/0. Bot repo untouched.
